message.content:
{
  "summary": "You present a relevant Australian reef-monitoring mission and use STK evidence to explore access and mission design. Your report has a clear structure, but errors in the launch-site latitude and orbit inclination undermine key conclusions. Strengthening the technical evidence, operational details, sourcing and final editing would make the design more persuasive and move the main-body, conclusion and presentation criteria toward the next rubric level.",
  "next_steps": [
    "In Launch, correct Kourou’s latitude and reassess the launch-window discussion. Verify the launch vehicle’s availability for your proposed timeframe and support feasibility with payload-interface, rideshare or injection information.",
    "In Orbit, use a retrograde inclination near 97.8° for a 600 km sun-synchronous orbit, then verify the RAAN and nodal-precession explanation. Add sensor parameters and quantitative coverage, revisit and imaging-performance analysis.",
    "In Ground Control & Communications and Mission Duration & EOL, show that link capacity supports the imagery and estimate drag-sail deployment and decay time. Clarify operator and customer organisations, strengthen and cross-check sources, and edit the incomplete EOL sentence and figure captions."
  ],
  "criteria": {
    "C1": "You explain the Australian reef-monitoring purpose, rationale and single-spacecraft choice in the Introduction. To strengthen this further, name the spacecraft operator and customer organisations, clarify their roles, and support the operational rationale with specific details and stronger sources.",
    "C2": "You use STK and provide orbit views and access results, addressing launch, orbit, communications, duration and disposal. The launch-site latitude and stated 87.79° inclination are incorrect, and coverage, link capacity, launch feasibility and disposal lifetime lack evidence. Correct these and add quantitative analyses and supporting files to reach Accomplished.",
    "C3": "Your Conclusion summarises the proposed mission and notes launch-vehicle uncertainty. To reach Accomplished, draw specific conclusions from verified design results, correct the orbit premise, and acknowledge analysis limitations rather than mainly restating the proposal.",
    "C4": "You provide an executive summary, recognisable engineering structure, figures, tables and a bibliography. To reach Accomplished, improve grammar and consistency, complete the EOL sentence, use clear numbered captions, and ensure in-text citations and references are complete, reliable and matched."
  }
}
